board type: Park / All Mountain
camber type: PurePop (evolution of traditional camber with subtle flat zones outside feet to amplify pop and add playful feeling, early rise tip and tail)
flex: 2.5/10
flex feel: Twin Flex (flexes the same in nose and tail)
shape: Twin (constructed exactly the same tip to tail)
core: Super Fly 800G (two species of wood in dual-density vertical laminations of alternating softwood and hardwood to reduce weight)
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core profile: Off-Axis Squeezebox Low (thicker powerful sections and thinner flexible sections at 15° angles matching park stance; Low version places stiffer zones outside feet for softer flex between bindings)
laminate: Womens Specific Triax Glass (triaxial fibreglass for versatile flex and consistent response)
base: Sintered (durable and highly porous for added strength and wax absorption)
mounting system: The Channel (compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
edges: Off-Axis Frostbite Edges (edges extend out slightly underneath bindings for enhanced edge hold on hardpack and ice)
tip/tail: Pro Tip (tip and tail taper out at points, reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin reducing carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
factory technology: Infinite Ride (boards overbuilt in factory then broken down by machinery to maintain consistent pop and performance from day one)
additional feature: EVA padding to absorb vibrations and smoothen ride for better stability
additional feature 2: Ultra thin core construction for lightness
shipping restriction: Only available for shipping within Australia
